<title>MEXICO: Pemex says sells 6.4 percent more diesel in 1996.</title>
<headline>Pemex says sells 6.4 percent more diesel in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's state-owned oil and gas monopoly Petroleos Mexicanos (Pemex) said Wednesday it sold an average 241,000 barrels per day (bpd) of diesel domestically in the first 10 months of the year, a 6.4 percent increase compared with the same period in 1995.</p>
<p>The nation's refineries produced an average 265,800 bpd of unsulfured and marine diesel in the time period, Pemex said in a statement.</p>
<p>Pemex refining from January to October sold 10,300 bpd in the international markets, the company said.</p>
<p>--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903</p>
</text>
